      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(usage): reject invalid UTF-8 in Anthropic and OpenAI admin usage responses",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readPage` in `extensions/anthropic/usage.ts` and `extensions/openai/usage.ts` decode the provider-controlled admin usage HTTP response with a non-fatal `new TextDecoder()`, which replaces invalid UTF-8 bytes with U+FFFD. `JSON.parse` then still succeeds on the mangled text, so a malformed usage response is silently aggregated into cost history as if it were valid usage, instead of being rejected.\n\nThe provider-controlled response is external (Anthropic/OpenAI admin billing API), so a corrupt or non-UTF-8 response should surface as a clean rejection, not as silently mangled usage accounting.\n\nMirror the sibling fix in `extensions/openrouter/usage.ts` (#111182), `extensions/venice/usage.ts` (#111180), and `extensions/clawrouter/usage.ts` (#111183): decode with `new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true })` so an invalid UTF-8 response throws. `readPage` is already wrapped in a `try/catch` that returns `{ ok: false }` on throw, so the response surfaces as `\"Usage unavailable\"` instead of producing corrupted usage data.\n\nNo shared usage-decode helper exists (each provider has its own inline `readPage`), so the OpenRouter/Venice/ClawRouter fatal-UTF-8 sweep did not cover the Anthropic and OpenAI admin usage readers.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The fix replaces `new TextDecoder().decode(buffer)` with `new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true }).decode(buffer)` in both `extensions/anthropic/usage.ts:143` and `extensions/openai/usage.ts:127`, identical to the one-line change in #111182 (`extensions/openrouter/usage.ts:84`).\n- New regression tests in `extensions/anthropic/usage.test.ts` and `extensions/openai/usage.test.ts`: each crafts an admin usage response body with an invalid UTF-8 byte (0xff) inside a JSON string field and asserts `result.error === \"Usage unavailable\"` with empty `windows`. With the old non-fatal decoder the byte would become U+FFFD, `JSON.parse` would still succeed, and the mangled bucket would be aggregated into cost history; the fatal decoder rejects it instead.\n- Local vitest run (Node v22.22.3, both files): `Test Files 2 passed (2)`, `Tests 17 passed (17)` (2 new invalid-UTF-8 regression tests + 15 existing, no regression).\n- `oxlint` on all four changed files: clean.\n\nSibling of #111180 / #111182 / #111183 (same non-fatal TextDecoder on a provider usage response, same fatal-decode fix); applies it to the Anthropic and OpenAI admin usage readers the sweep missed. Combined into one PR because the two readers are byte-identical in shape and there is no shared helper to fix once.",
        "branch": "fix/anthropic-openai-usage-fatal-utf8",
        "head_sha": "80a8563a959a31a87e822857025074c2ff876a12",
